{"parentUuid":"a728e1c9-d1d9-40a0-8795-dd236883fd7f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"20bcfc03-9a21-4d08-9f1c-8f35b9ed4281","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. macOS primary since 2026-08-05; Windows 11 still active. Tool paths: CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\\n- **Status report**: #3 by 9/25, biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: phone check; host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 + Sprint Film Check built. NEXT: Tim/Jacob → export; Joe notes → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; run 9/29. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: K-B self-audit done. Ship to a named user q2wk: RI5 #002 (`_v2` only) wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. Wk4 COLO: EPA layer only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/26)**: 013 built; size Q + 011 await Mauro (asst GM). →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\\n- **TypeSafe (9/28)**: Drive triage FAIL 76.5%; Jev>Haiku, used for Flint. PR #31 draft; Eric audit. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\\n- **Flint (9/28)**: interview done+applied. NEXT Eric: shortlists, primer, CVASPS. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. Both: 2026 thru wk3 + video. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Hooks: patch both copies only for shared events; Codex has no prompt-submit event. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: `Desktop\\\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches/worktrees unasked (verify first) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **OKR gate (9/14)**: AI buy-in + data governance (Anthony = outside-firm adviser, NOT Mauro). NCAA charter or park?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n- **memsearch-sync** ×30 (2026-09-28 00:05 → 2026-09-28 17:48 UTC): index ETIMEDOUT 35x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\n- **compiler-stale-lock** ×4 (2026-09-23 01:01 → 2026-09-28 03:46 UTC): reclaimed compile lock held 121min by pid 109324 (compile.py --auto)\\n- **compiler-flush-failed** ×10 (2026-09-27 17:32 → 2026-09-28 04:47 UTC): memory-compiler flush failed (session codex-01a0e43b-bff1-71a1-8797-6383c003b75c): **Context:** Force Plate Practitioner course archiving project (Applied Performance community course) — completing the video archive and Zotero library import, continued from a prior Codex session.  * | a single failu…\\n- **compiler-backlog** ×3 (2026-09-23 01:01 → 2026-09-25 02:25 UTC): 2 log(s) backlogged, compiling newest 2 this run - run compile.py manually to catch up\\n- **daily-backup** ×7 (2026-09-23 07:53 → 2026-09-30 07:51 UTC): 1 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n- **perch-pull** ×2 (2026-09-26 16:26 → 2026-09-27 00:34 UTC): error exit=1 after 3 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026/logs/last_run.json\\n- **adjudicate-budget-tripped** ×1 (2026-09-27 16:06 → 2026-09-27 16:06 UTC): stopped after 315,063 / 250,000 tokens\\n- **vald-pull** ×1 (2026-09-28 19:02 → 2026-09-28 19:02 UTC): error exit=1 after 2 attempt(s) — see /Users/kristinarash/DEV/ForcePlate_DecisionSystem/logs/last_run.json\\n- 10 unparsed line(s); see the file.\\n\\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4335 chars, updated 2026-09-30 11:14)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":672},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3ba452b0-3207-42c4-a83d-17d04dc1cc73","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:33:41.265Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3ba452b0-3207-42c4-a83d-17d04dc1cc73","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"20bcfc03-9a21-4d08-9f1c-8f35b9ed4281","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nWednesday, September 30, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n310 compiled articles (230 concepts, 79 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n# Daily Log: 2026-09-30\\n\\n## Sessions\\n\\n## Memory Maintenance\\n\\n### Memory Flush (11:29)\\n\\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":677},"type":"attachment","uuid":"affa7297-f168-44e6-bbcf-661e7908aa17","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:33:41.268Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"affa7297-f168-44e6-bbcf-661e7908aa17","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"20bcfc03-9a21-4d08-9f1c-8f35b9ed4281","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":779},"type":"attachment","uuid":"70bce870-5f42-41ab-ada1-1ad9b09376ac","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:33:41.373Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
