{"parentUuid":"4d507be2-8510-4130-8abd-ba2623098aec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZx7uGowVYJqGTbeH3zy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":96248,"output_tokens":2762,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1406},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":96248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZx7tsFquxYuBXNNaJwx","attributionSkill":"claude-stack-doctor","type":"assistant","uuid":"373a5118-8df1-487b-bea8-7e1f685b984c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:37:37.165Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"373a5118-8df1-487b-bea8-7e1f685b984c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZx7uGowVYJqGTbeH3zy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Health check is done. The memory sync problem is fixed. Your cleanup list is below.\n\n## Part 1: Stack health\n\n**I fixed:**\n- Memory on this Mac was 13 commits behind the Windows laptop, so this session started with old memory.\n- The pull was blocked because both machines wrote to the same daily logs. I committed the Mac copies, merged them with the Windows copies (kept both sides), and pushed.\n- The re-check now says `HANDOFF HEALTHY`.\n- The same block caused the `daily-backup` error (`repo-behind-blocked:global-memory`). It should clear after tonight's 21:00 run.\n\n**These cleared by themselves:**\n- The `vald-pull` and `perch-pull` errors: both ran OK this morning.\n- The 9/27 flush error: that session hit the usage limit. It is not a fault.\n\n**You need to do this:**\n1. The Google Drive check fails because the `gws` login has expired. Run this yourself, then open the URL it prints:\n   `! gws auth login --scopes \"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly\"`\n   Then run: `rm ~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n2. `MEMORY.md` is 98% full. Remove a few old threads soon.\n\nI did not clear `.errors.log`. The login fix is still open.\n\n## Part 2: What you actually use (last 60 days)\n\n**Tools you use:** Chrome (686 calls), context-mode (104), Zotero (74), Firecrawl (48), Drive (19), Fireflies (16), Gmail, Calendar.\n\n**Never used, so cut them:**\n\n| Item | Uses | Why cut |\n|---|---|---|\n| `data` plugin (Amplitude, Atlassian, Hex, Definite) | 0 | Definite fails to connect every session. |\n| Supabase connector | 0 | It has write tools, like create and delete, that you never use. That is a risk with no benefit. |\n| HyperFrames, Excalidraw connectors | 0 | Not used. |\n| Desktop Commander | 1 | Bash does the same job. On Windows it slows startup by 23–46 s. |\n| browser-use | 1 | Chrome already covers it. |\n| exa | 0 | Firecrawl already covers it. |\n| pdf-viewer, cowork-plugin-management | 0 | Not used. |\n\n**Skills you load twice:**\n- The `anthropic-skills` pack has copies of your own `closeout`, `dev-sync`, `new-project`, `five-slides-generator`, `watch` and `last30days`.\n- `last30days` loads 3 ways.\n- `mattpocock-skills` is synced twice and is also turned on as a plugin.\n- The Firecrawl plugin adds 13 skills. You only use the Firecrawl connector, which works without them.\n\n**Your own skills with 0 uses in 60 days:** `anti-sleep`, `ArXiv`, `ISA`, `Science`, `capture-insight`, `claudex-route`, `cli-hub-meta-skill`, `codex-build`, `design-taste-frontend` (plus a `-v1` copy), `harvest`, `improve-system`, `library-advisor`, `library-review`, `next-decision`, `persistent-localhost`, `project-triage`, `session-miner`.\n- Keep `brain-audit`, `weekly-review`, `pbir-report-builder` and `pp-catapult-openfield-connect`. Scheduled jobs or rare but real tasks may need them.\n\n## What you decide\n\nThe connectors and synced plugins can only be removed on claude.ai, under Settings → Connectors and Customize → Plugins. That part is yours. Your own skills are the part I can change:\n\n- **Option A:** I turn off the 17 unused skills in `settings.json`. Nothing is deleted, and one line brings each one back.\n- **Option B:** Leave them.\n\nI recommend **A**. It removes about a third of the skill list that loads into every session, and it is easy to undo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":96248,"output_tokens":2762,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1406},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":96248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfZx7tsFquxYuBXNNaJwx","attributionSkill":"claude-stack-doctor","type":"assistant","uuid":"44c7fee4-0e6c-4b5f-84bd-26480e1e2437","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:37:41.550Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
