{"parentUuid":"87389df8-cd27-4747-9c0a-3bf0d6ebddf2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZxdZ7wtiSBh5V5MZE4i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did not change anything yet. Option A would save much less than I said.\n\n**Why:**\n- All 17 unused skills are already set to `name-only` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. Only their names load, not their full descriptions.\n- Switching them to `off` would save only about 17 short names.\n- It also carries a risk: an `off` skill may stop working when you type it, for example `/harvest`.\n- I said this would cut about a third of your skill list. That was wrong.\n\n**The cleanup that actually matters is on claude.ai.** Only you can do it:\n1. claude.ai → Settings → Connectors. Remove Supabase, HyperFrames and Excalidraw.\n2. claude.ai → Customize → Plugins. Remove `data`, Desktop Commander, browser-use, exa, pdf-viewer, cowork-plugin-management and the second mattpocock copy.\n\nEach of these loads tool lists into every session, and the `data` plugin fails to connect on every start.\n\n**Google login:** the page is open in your browser now.\n1. Sign in and approve access.\n2. Tell me when you are done. I will delete the old token and check that the Drive check passes.\n\n**What you decide:**\n- **Option A:** Set the 17 skills to `off` anyway. The gain is very small.\n- **Option B:** Leave them as `name-only` and do the claude.ai cleanup above.\n\nI recommend **B**."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":102500,"output_tokens":460,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":750,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":46