{"parentUuid":"a704287b-5608-47a3-a026-990dd31886aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZxitTvXz6njRE4zbxpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019YKY94DV1SMszDFvezsRA1","name":"Skill","input":{"skill":"memory-write","args":"Update project_tech-inventory-refresh.md (Tier A, ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/): 2026-09-30 gws auth is broken by an invalid OAuth client SECRET, not token rot. `gws auth login` fails with \"invalid_client: The provided client secret is invalid\" for client 208643585660-3ogm… in ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json (dated 2026-06-19). Re-auth alone will not fix it: need a new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) from Google Cloud Console → Credentials, save over client_secret.json, then login, then delete token_cache.json. Eric chose to defer 9/30. Blocks the stack-doctor backup-cloud-check and the tech-inventory refresh (due 9/29)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":106725,"output_tokens":530,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":152},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":106725,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019YKY94DV1SMszDFvezsRA1":{"skill":"memory-write","args":"Update project_tech-inventory-refresh.md (Tier A, ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/): 2026-09-30 gws auth is broken by an invalid OAuth client SECRET, not token rot. `gws auth login` fails with \"invalid_client: The provided client secret is invalid\" for client 208643585660-3ogm… in ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json (dated 2026-06-19). Re-auth alone will not fix it: need a new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) from Google Cloud Console → Credentials, save over client_secret.json, then login, then delete token_cache.json. Eric chose to defer 9/30. Blocks the stack-doctor backup-cloud-check and the tech-inventory refresh (due 9/29)."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfZxisPS8X2zP926XvP2m","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c0d82d4-708a-47dc-92e6-cf5c9efa95e4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:15.310Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8c0d82d4-708a-47dc-92e6-cf5c9efa95e4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b90f8b94-e2d8-4581-bd2e-f5087d776165","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_019YKY94DV1SMszDFvezsRA1","content":"Launching skill: memory-write"}]},"uuid":"1834e21b-992c-4e1c-9a50-3e5b11dcb61c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:15.425Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"commandName":"memory-write"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c0d82d4-708a-47dc-92e6-cf5c9efa95e4","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"1834e21b-992c-4e1c-9a50-3e5b11dcb61c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b90f8b94-e2d8-4581-bd2e-f5087d776165","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/memory-write\n\n# Memory Write\n\n## Outcome\n- Fact added to, updated in, or removed from the correct memory tier\n- Tier-B caps enforced (2,500 chars for MEMORY.md, 1,375 for USER.md)\n- Confirmation: \"Saved — will be active from next session.\"\n\n## Pick the tier first\n\nAsk: \"Will this fact still be true and useful in 3 months, across multiple projects?\"\n\n**Tier A — `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`** (one file per fact, indexed by MEMORY.md)\n- Durable user facts → `user_*.md` (metadata.type: user)\n- Stable project conventions / gotchas → `project_*.md` (metadata.type: project)\n- Behavioral feedback rules → `feedback_*.md` (metadata.type: feedback)\n- External-system pointers → `reference_*.md` (metadata.type: reference)\n\n**Tier B — `~/.claude/global-memory/`** (single capped file)\n- Active threads (in-progress work) → `MEMORY.md` `## Active Threads`\n- Current env notes (URLs, tool versions, project structure in play) → `MEMORY.md` `## Environment Notes`\n- Pending decisions → `MEMORY.md` `## Pending Decisions`\n- Durable user profile updates → `USER.md`\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Decide tier** using the rule above.\n2. **Read** the target file in full.\n3. **Dedup check** — substring scan; if the fact already exists, skip or update in place.\n4. **Cap check** for Tier B — `wc -c < ~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md` (or USER.md). If over cap, consolidate (merge similar entries, prune stale) before adding.\n5. **Write** the change.\n   - Tier A: create a new file with proper frontmatter (name, description, metadata.type) and add a one-line pointer to that slug's `MEMORY.md` index. `name:` follows the rule below.\n   - Tier B: append under the correct `##` section.\n6. **Confirm** in one line: `Saved — will be active from next session.`\n\n## The `name:` field — bare kebab slug\n\n**`name:` = the filename stem minus its leading type token, kebab-cased.** The type\nalready lives in `metadata.type` and the filename already carries the prefix; repeating\nit in `name:` is the third copy.\n\n| File | `name:` |\n|---|---|\n| `project_automation-cadence.md` | `automation-cadence` |\n| `user_sports-teams.md` | `sports-teams` |\n| `reference_baylor-house-style.md` | `baylor-house-style` |\n| `feedback_project_idea_capture.md` | `project-idea-capture` |\n\nNote the last row: strip only the **leading** token. `feedback_project_idea_capture.md`\nis a feedback memory *about* project-idea capture — its name keeps the word `project`.\n\n`[[links]]` target this bare name, never the filename and never a prefixed variant.\n\nThis rule exists because it was previously unwritten: an audit on 2026-09-02 found the\ncorpus split 59 bare / 58 prefixed, which broke 37 links. Both forms look right in\nisolation, so without a stated rule the split regrows on every write.\n\n## Actions\n\n- **add** — append (default)\n- **replace** — substring match + swap. Preferred over add when updating an existing fact.\n- **remove** — confirm with the user before deleting.\n\n## Retrieval — the tiered ladder\n\nWhen the user asks about past context, decisions, or \"did we already…?\", climb in order and stop as soon as the question is answered. Do not run memsearch when the answer is already in the injected snapshot.\n\n1. **Tier 0** — scan what is already in context (USER.md, MEMORY.md, today's compiled log). Zero cost.\n2. **L1** — `memsearch search \"query\" --top-k 5`. Hybrid vector + keyword across all indexed paths: Tier A files (including the Windows-machine slugs), daily logs, transcripts.\n3. **L2** — `memsearch expand <chunk_hash>`. Full markdown section around a hit.\n4. **L3** — `memsearch transcript <session_id>`. Raw dialogue. Last resort.\n5. **Fallback** — say \"I don't have a record of that.\"\n\n## Daily compiled logs — read-only\n\n`~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md` is produced by `claude-memory-compiler` through its own SessionEnd/PreCompact hooks, and injected by its own SessionStart hook.\n\n- **Never hand-edit these files.** The compiler owns them.\n- **Never read them eagerly.** Treat the injected snapshot as the source of truth.\n\n## What is loaded at session start\n\n`~/.claude/global-memory/USER.md` and `MEMORY.md` are read once at session start and are a **frozen snapshot**. Mid-session writes persist to disk but only take effect next session — this is deliberate, to preserve the prefix cache. Never load more than the startup set proactively.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Never exceed Tier B caps. Consolidate first.\n- Always dedup before adding.\n- For Tier A, the slug is the current cwd with `/` and `.` replaced by `-` (so `~` → `-Users-kristinarash`, `~/DEV` → `-Users-kristinarash-DEV`, `~/.claude/skills` → `-Users-kristinarash--claude-skills`). The harness injects the correct slug each session — use that, don't reconstruct it.\n- **Write only to the current machine's slug.** Both machines are active as of 2026-09-10: Mac slugs are `-Users-kristinarash-*`, Windows slugs are `C--Users-eric-rash-*`. A fact written to the other machine's slug is never auto-injected here (memsearch still finds it). Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n- Never announce the write mid-session beyond the one-line confirmation. The injected snapshot is frozen — the new fact appears next session, not this one.\n\n## Verification Gate\n\nAfter every write:\n\n1. Read the exact destination back and require the intended fact to appear once in the intended tier.\n2. Re-run the Tier B character cap check after the write.\n3. Check the surrounding section for an unresolved contradiction or stale duplicate. Resolve it or report `FAIL`.\n4. For Tier A, verify the new file has valid frontmatter and the memory index pointer resolves to it.\n5. Distinguish persisted state from activation: the write can pass now, but next-session injection remains unverified until a later session observes it.\n\nReport `PASS` only when persistence, uniqueness, tier placement, caps, and pointers are verified. Report `FAIL` with the target path and failed check otherwise. Do not emit “Saved” before read-back succeeds.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Update project_tech-inventory-refresh.md (Tier A, ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/): 2026-09-30 gws auth is broken by an invalid OAuth client SECRET, not token rot. `gws auth login` fails with \"invalid_client: The provided client secret is invalid\" for client 208643585660-3ogm… in ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json (dated 2026-06-19). Re-auth alone will not fix it: need a new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) from Google Cloud Console → Credentials, save over client_secret.json, then login, then delete token_cache.json. Eric chose to defer 9/30. Blocks the stack-doctor backup-cloud-check and the tech-inventory refresh (due 9/29)."}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"947ddb42-fd14-4344-a654-2648e0d24c59","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:15.341Z","sourceToolUseID":"toolu_019YKY94DV1SMszDFvezsRA1","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
