{"parentUuid":"905c5d9f-6445-4824-8d2b-77ac018eed6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZxjLRNtRqVDiv56qetV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JoTSZFhC3BgXSxd5fnjLam","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_tech-inventory-refresh.md; grep -n \"gws\\|invalid_client\" ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md | head","description":"Read the target memory file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3227,"cache_read_input_tokens":107105,"output_tokens":171,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3227,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":107105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3227},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JoTSZFhC3BgXSxd5fnjLam":{"command":"cat ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_tech-inventory-refresh.md; grep -n \"gws\\|invalid_client\" ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md | head","description":"Read the target memory file"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZxjL15F7J9mupB1zK9g","attributionSkill":"memory-write","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea607b99-98bf-4f52-bb9f-bb3c9419d5cf","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:17.248Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ea607b99-98bf-4f52-bb9f-bb3c9419d5cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b90f8b94-e2d8-4581-bd2e-f5087d776165","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JoTSZFhC3BgXSxd5fnjLam","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: tech-inventory-refresh\ndescription: \"Baylor Tech Inventory survey — 09-15 baseline, how to pull the live responses, the renumbered-ID trap, and the Business Office proxy entries\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3101f63e-ae24-43b1-9f12-b3bcdc82bdcc\n  modified: 2026-09-16T20:55:38.440Z\n---\n\nAnalysis repo: `~/Desktop/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis` — **a git repo** (erash11,\nprivate). Supersedes the Mac-slug note of the same name, which still says \"not a\ngit repo\" and has the 08-29 baseline.\n\n**Latest run 2026-09-16** (merged to `main` 2026-09-16, commit `6edf470`): 52\nresponses, **Volleyball answered for itself → 32 of 32 units**, 188 products, 75\nathlete-data, 123 single-unit, 9 retired, 18 BO-only (VB confirmed Hawkin +\nDVSport outside the form → `UNIT_CONFIRMED` in `aliases.py`). Write-up\n`docs/FINDINGS_2026-09-16.md`. The fresh Forms download lands as\n`...Inventory(1-NN).xlsx` in Downloads; the OneDrive-synced copy did not update.\n\n**Previous baseline 2026-09-15** (merged to `main` 2026-09-15): 51\nresponses, 31 of 32 units answering for themselves, **Volleyball covered only by a\nBusiness Office entry**, 185 products, 75 athlete-data candidates, 9 retirements.\nWrite-up `docs/FINDINGS_2026-09-15.md`; deliverables dated 2026-09-15.\n\n**Getting the data.** Live survey is Microsoft Forms. The Forms page's download\nmenu sits in an iframe the browser tool cannot click; Eric downloaded the\nOneDrive-synced workbook `Athletics Technology - Quick Inventory.xlsx` himself.\n\n**Trap — renumbered IDs.** That synced workbook heads the column `Id`, has no\n`Last modified time`, and renumbers responses (StatCrew went 5 → 3). Match\nresponses across exports on start + completion time; compare products on\nunit × product, never by diffing `clean/`.\n\n**Trap — Business Office proxies.** One Business Office respondent entered vendor\nlists for 11 units (2 in August, 9 on 9/14) plus a department-wide contract list.\n`clean_inventory.py` tags these `source=business-office`; coverage status\n`BUSINESS OFFICE ONLY` marks a unit whose own staff never answered.\n\n**Refresh:** save as `raw/Quick_Inventory_export_YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx`, run\n`clean_inventory.py`, loop `unmapped_review.csv` into `aliases.py`, then the three\nbuilders (`build_docx.py`, `build_exec_summary.py`, `build_tech_lists.py`) — they run\non Windows via Word COM. Update `PREVIOUS` in `build_docx.py` each run.\n\n**Why:** the ID renumbering makes a naive diff report every row as changed, and the\nproxy entries would otherwise read as 100% coverage.\n\n**How to apply:** before the post-9/29 final run, merge the refresh branch first.\nRelated: [[ath-tech-framework]], [[baylor-house-style]].\n3:description: \"Standing automation schedule on the Mac — ritual nudges, memsearch reindex timing, OS audit cadence, gws/Gmail capability limits, reMarkable OCR entry point\"\n40:- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n41:  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n42:  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cdade331-75d2-40cf-8a56-15f59a1c31d7","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:17.465Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: tech-inventory-refresh\ndescription: \"Baylor Tech Inventory survey — 09-15 baseline, how to pull the live responses, the renumbered-ID trap, and the Business Office proxy entries\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3101f63e-ae24-43b1-9f12-b3bcdc82bdcc\n  modified: 2026-09-16T20:55:38.440Z\n---\n\nAnalysis repo: `~/Desktop/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis` — **a git repo** (erash11,\nprivate). Supersedes the Mac-slug note of the same name, which still says \"not a\ngit repo\" and has the 08-29 baseline.\n\n**Latest run 2026-09-16** (merged to `main` 2026-09-16, commit `6edf470`): 52\nresponses, **Volleyball answered for itself → 32 of 32 units**, 188 products, 75\nathlete-data, 123 single-unit, 9 retired, 18 BO-only (VB confirmed Hawkin +\nDVSport outside the form → `UNIT_CONFIRMED` in `aliases.py`). Write-up\n`docs/FINDINGS_2026-09-16.md`. The fresh Forms download lands as\n`...Inventory(1-NN).xlsx` in Downloads; the OneDrive-synced copy did not update.\n\n**Previous baseline 2026-09-15** (merged to `main` 2026-09-15): 51\nresponses, 31 of 32 units answering for themselves, **Volleyball covered only by a\nBusiness Office entry**, 185 products, 75 athlete-data candidates, 9 retirements.\nWrite-up `docs/FINDINGS_2026-09-15.md`; deliverables dated 2026-09-15.\n\n**Getting the data.** Live survey is Microsoft Forms. The Forms page's download\nmenu sits in an iframe the browser tool cannot click; Eric downloaded the\nOneDrive-synced workbook `Athletics Technology - Quick Inventory.xlsx` himself.\n\n**Trap — renumbered IDs.** That synced workbook heads the column `Id`, has no\n`Last modified time`, and renumbers responses (StatCrew went 5 → 3). Match\nresponses across exports on start + completion time; compare products on\nunit × product, never by diffing `clean/`.\n\n**Trap — Business Office proxies.** One Business Office respondent entered vendor\nlists for 11 units (2 in August, 9 on 9/14) plus a department-wide contract list.\n`clean_inventory.py` tags these `source=business-office`; coverage status\n`BUSINESS OFFICE ONLY` marks a unit whose own staff never answered.\n\n**Refresh:** save as `raw/Quick_Inventory_export_YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx`, run\n`clean_inventory.py`, loop `unmapped_review.csv` into `aliases.py`, then the three\nbuilders (`build_docx.py`, `build_exec_summary.py`, `build_tech_lists.py`) — they run\non Windows via Word COM. Update `PREVIOUS` in `build_docx.py` each run.\n\n**Why:** the ID renumbering makes a naive diff report every row as changed, and the\nproxy entries would otherwise read as 100% coverage.\n\n**How to apply:** before the post-9/29 final run, merge the refresh branch first.\nRelated: [[ath-tech-framework]], [[baylor-house-style]].\n3:description: \"Standing automation schedule on the Mac — ritual nudges, memsearch reindex timing, OS audit cadence, gws/Gmail capability limits, reMarkable OCR entry point\"\n40:- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n41:  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n42:  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea607b99-98bf-4f52-bb9f-bb3c9419d5cf","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
