{"parentUuid":"b9fec219-5fd5-4137-a70c-9dfbaccdd33e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZxjmGrRaKCxqjPvW4wV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0164eLHLjnmEbgnAA5Siphud","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md","old_string":"- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].","new_string":"- **gws is BROKEN since 2026-09-30 (deferred by Eric).** Login fails `invalid_client: The\n  provided client secret is invalid` for client `208643585660-3ogm…` in\n  `~/.config/gws/client_secret.json` (dated 2026-06-19). This is the OAuth client secret,\n  not token rot — re-auth alone will not fix it. Fix: Google Cloud Console → Credentials →\n  new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) → save over `client_secret.json` → login →\n  delete `token_cache.json`. Until then stack-doctor reports `backup-cloud-check`.\n- **gws** re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":111920,"output_tokens":560,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":560,"cache_