{"parentUuid":"e01448e6-a43d-4def-bb2b-b834e8e463a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b90f8b94-e2d8-4581-bd2e-f5087d776165","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0164eLHLjnmEbgnAA5Siphud","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"1aee57b6-6253-45c3-b2aa-e51e77ac1743","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:45:25.855Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md","oldString":"- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].","newString":"- **gws is BROKEN since 2026-09-30 (deferred by Eric).** Login fails `invalid_client: The\n  provided client secret is invalid` for client `208643585660-3ogm…` in\n  `~/.config/gws/client_secret.json` (dated 2026-06-19). This is the OAuth client secret,\n  not token rot — re-auth alone will not fix it. Fix: Google Cloud Console → Credentials →\n  new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) → save over `client_secret.json` → login →\n  delete `token_cache.json`. Until then stack-doctor reports `backup-cloud-check`.\n- **gws** re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].","originalFile":"---\nname: automation-cadence\ndescription: \"Standing automation schedule on the Mac — ritual nudges, memsearch reindex timing, OS audit cadence, gws/Gmail capability limits, reMarkable OCR entry point\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 330c1f71-242a-47c7-ac7b-129bd6f5dd3c\n  modified: 2026-08-14T20:15:14.244Z\n---\n\nDurable schedule and capability facts for the Mac automation stack. These are stable\nsettings, not active threads — health-check them with `/claude-stack-doctor`.\n\n## Ritual nudges (launchd `com.keystone.rituals`)\n\n- **Weekdays 17:00** → `/interview-me`\n- **Fridays 15:30** → `/weekly-review`\n- `harvest` and `forecast-capture` also run through `ritual-check.ps1`; their\n  due/overdue state is computed from their own output, not from a fixed clock\n  (forecast-capture is Monday-anchored and season-bounded — see\n  [[cfb-forecast-capture]]). Four rituals total; `Name    = ` in\n  `KeystoneOS/scripts/ritual-check.ps1` is the authoritative list.\n\nThe nudge is only a prompt; **the output artifact is the record**, not the reminder firing.\n\n## memsearch reindex\n\nReindex **rides the daily backup task** rather than running on its own timer. The\nnightly moved 00:30 → **09:00 on 2026-08-29** (CRASHBOX was unplugged at 00:30), so\nany reasoning that assumes an overnight reindex is wrong — the backup's uncapped full reindex absorbs backlogs the\nshort SessionEnd hook can't finish. See [[backup-sync-system]].\n\n## OS audits\n\nFull OS audit last run **2026-07-24** (reports under `audits/`, guards auto-run);\n**next due 2026-10-24**.\n\n## Capability limits worth remembering\n\n- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`\n  shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`\n  must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]].\n- **MCP Gmail is draft-only** — it can compose drafts but must not be treated as a send path.\n\n## reMarkable OCR\n\n`remarkable_extract.py` — USB-first with a `--cloud` fallback; Vision API key lives in\n`.env`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 330c1f71-242a-47c7-ac7b-129bd6f5dd3c","-  modified: 2026-08-14T20:15:14.244Z","+  modified: 2026-09-30T16:45:25.775Z"," ---"," "," Durable schedule and capability facts for the Mac automation stack. These are stable"]},{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":7,"newStart":37,"newLines":13,"lines":[" "," ## Capability limits worth remembering"," ","-- **gws** is authenticated. Re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`","+- **gws is BROKEN since 2026-09-30 (deferred by Eric).** Login fails `invalid_client: The","+  provided client secret is invalid` for client `208643585660-3ogm…` in","+  `~/.config/gws/client_secret.json` (dated 2026-06-19). This is the OAuth client secret,","+  not token rot — re-auth alone will not fix it. Fix: Google Cloud Console → Credentials →","+  new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) → save over `client_secret.json` → login →","+  delete `token_cache.json`. Until then stack-doctor reports `backup-cloud-check`.","+- **gws** re-auth requires explicit full scope URLs — the `-s drive`","   shorthand silently grants no scopes (v0.22.5 bug), and `~/.config/gws/token_cache.json`","   must be deleted after re-auth or the stale token is served. See [[gws-forms-api]]."," - **MCP Gmail is draft-only** — it can compose drafts but must not be treated as a send path."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e01448e6-a43d-4def-bb2b-b834e8e463a2","session_id":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"b3c359e3-93aa-4828-9267-d061a2907833","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
