{"parentUuid":"3a3254a3-9024-4aca-9e7f-66c55ca95477","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZysRJ9wpMbAeVJJ491e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mu7gx4e79X2xZh2NJqpGe3","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_automation-cadence.md","old_string":"- **gws is BROKEN since 2026-09-30 (deferred by Eric).** Login fails `invalid_client: The\n  provided client secret is invalid` for client `208643585660-3ogm…` in\n  `~/.config/gws/client_secret.json` (dated 2026-06-19). This is the OAuth client secret,\n  not token rot — re-auth alone will not fix it. Fix: Google Cloud Console → Credentials →\n  new secret (or new Desktop OAuth client) → save over `client_secret.json` → login →\n  delete `token_cache.json`. Until then stack-doctor reports `backup-cloud-check`.","new_string":"- **gws `invalid_client: The provided client secret is invalid` = stale client SECRET, not\n  token rot** — re-auth alone never fixes it. The secret for client `208643585660-3ogm…`\n  (project `baylor-gws`) was rotated 2026-09-17 to one ending `Xyjf`; the Mac kept the\n  June one until 2026-09-30, when the Windows copy was carried over via Drive. Console no\n  longer shows or downloads a secret: copy the other machine's `client_secret.json`, or\n  Add secret (shown once). Then login, then delete `token_cache.json`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":139462,"output_tokens":643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":66},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":