{"parentUuid":"2dac2e6c-7154-489b-bcf9-4931c78e2788","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZytrhedMgoNDRjSV8KC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`gws` works again on this Mac. A test Drive query returned a file, and the backup cloud check now passes.\n\n**What fixed it:** the key on this Mac was old.\n- Someone replaced the key in Google Cloud on 9/17. This Mac kept the June key.\n- The Windows file had the new key. You moved it here through Drive, then logged in.\n\n**Other cleanup:**\n- The memory note now says what went wrong and how to fix it, not \"broken\".\n- I archived `.errors.log` as `.errors.log.archived-2026-09-30b`, then cleared it.\n\n**Health check:** 6 issues at the start, 2 now.\n- `backup-error`: should clear after tonight's 21:00 backup. The cause (stale memory) is fixed.\n- `flush-error`: comes from the 9/27 daily log, when the flush hit the usage limit. It clears when that log ages out of the check. No fix is needed.\n\n**Still for you, when you have time:**\n- The claude.ai cleanup: remove the unused connectors and plugins from the list earlier.\n- Empty Google Drive's Trash so the copy of the key is gone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":140607,"output_tokens":373,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":548,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":140607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":548},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nul